Description: ZFS bare-metal backup and recovery suite for Ubuntu
 zark provides full bare-metal backup and disaster recovery for Ubuntu
 systems running on encrypted ZFS root pools (rpool/bpool with a LUKS
 keystore zvol). Backups are written to external drives via syncoid raw
 send, preserving native ZFS encryption end-to-end.
 .
 The recover command performs a full system restoration from a live USB
 in approximately one minute, reconstructing rpool, bpool, the LUKS
 keystore, GRUB and initramfs without touching the source system.
 .
 zark is portable: it can also be run directly from a USB pendrive
 without installation, which is the recommended workflow for disaster
 recovery scenarios. The Debian package is intended for system-wide
 installation on machines where zark drives the day-to-day backup
 routine.
